@startuml
title Missed CNI DEL versus Kubernetes API outage | implemented contract
autonumber
skinparam backgroundColor #FCFCFD
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName DejaVu Sans
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam maxMessageSize 180
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #2F5D7C
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #EAF4FF

actor "Fixture / lifecycle authority" as T
participant "Node-Agent\ncontinuity / orphan scan" as A
database "Durable CNI journal\nactive ACK + exact receipts" as J
participant "Kubernetes API" as K
participant "Owned OVN / OVS\nobjects + host link" as R
participant "Type-2 exporter /\nGoBGP" as E

note over T,E
  Explanatory implemented path; dedicated operational acceptance is incomplete.
  The agent/speaker restart profiles do not inject these two scenarios.
end note

A -> J : reopen matching ownership domain;\nreplay pending orphan intent before other ACKs
== Distinct retirement and uncertainty branches ==
alt confirmed Pod retirement, DEL withheld
  T -> K : retire original Pod; independently confirm exact UID
  A -> K : verify Node identity and original Pod retirement
  K --> A : definitive NotFound or replacement Pod UID
  A -> J : persist cni-orphan-del with matching active ACK
  A -> K : revalidate retirement immediately before deletion
  K --> A : original Pod still retired
  A -> R : delete exact receipt-owned OVS objects,\nthen exact owned OVN LSP; verify DB absence
  R --> A : matching DB objects absent
  A -> R : read host-link absence only
  alt host absence verified
    A -> J : commit deleted acknowledgement
  else host remains or host absence uncertain
    A -> J : commit orphan_host_unresolved + reason
    A -> A : never delete orphan host veth;\nretain unresolved ownership for investigation
  end
  A -> A : remove retired endpoint from active store
  E -> A : validate continuity and authoritative desired endpoints
  note over A,E
    Export reconciliation is separately gated by current authority,
    complete observations, journal state and exact path receipts.
    Orphan cleanup is not an unconditional BGP withdrawal command.
  end note
else Kubernetes API unavailable / incomplete identity evidence
  T -> K : inject API unavailability separately
  A -> K : current Pod / Node observation
  K --> A : error, not Pod retirement
  A -> A : report observation failure; preserve unresolved state
  A -> E : no authorized empty snapshot from API error
  E -> E : retain owned advertisements; block unsafe mutation
  note over A,R
    No withdrawal, adoption or cleanup authority from API error,
    deletion timestamp alone, or missing sandbox/netns.
  end note
end

== Qualification requires separate before/after evidence ==
T -> J : compare intents, ACKs and ownership domain
T -> R : verify exact owned absence / unresolved host;\nindependently compare foreign survivors
T -> E : compare path receipts and actual routes;\ncheck later forwarding and scoped cleanup where permitted

legend bottom center
  Source contract and offline tests, not live run results.
  Unknown resources and replacement workloads must not be adopted or deleted.
endlegend
@enduml
